  ('MU-IFRS-IS', 'MU', 'default', 'Statement of profit or loss', 'income_statement', 'IFRS', date '2015-09-15', null, 'Financial Reporting Act 2004, s. 72 and s. 75(1); IAS 1 asks for a statement of profit or loss, and allows the expenses to be analysed by nature, which these lines follow.', 'fra-2004'),
  ('MU-IFRS-SFP', 'MU', 'default', 'Statement of financial position', 'balance_sheet', 'IFRS', date '2015-09-15', null, 'Financial Reporting Act 2004, s. 72 and s. 75(1) — standards consistent with IFRS apply to the financial statements of a public interest entity, and the Financial Reporting Council''s framework page applies standards consistent with IFRS to the other companies; IAS 1 requires a statement of financial position that separates current from non-current assets and liabilities. The lines below follow the presentation of the IFRS for SMEs and IAS 1, which a company that is not a public interest entity may apply.', 'fra-2004')
